# 2. Scope Discipline

This is a UX refinement task.

Do not change:

- TVMaze API integration;
- TanStack Query architecture;
- Favorites persistence architecture;
- DTO/domain models unless required for presentation only;
- search behavior;
- filtering semantics;
- navigation routes;
- state ownership;
- tests unrelated to modified behavior.

Do not perform unrelated refactors.

---

# 3. Home Header — Safe Area

The current Home header visually overlaps or sits too close to the device notification/status area.

Fix the layout so the Home content correctly respects the top safe area.

The final layout must not overlap:

- status bar;
- notification area;
- device cutout/notch.

Use the existing Expo/React Native safe-area setup.

Do not introduce another safe-area dependency.

Avoid applying safe-area padding twice if the current navigation layer already handles part of it.

---

# 4. Home Header — Visual Hierarchy

Improve the top area of Home.

Desired hierarchy:

```text
safe area

      Show Explorer
         centered

search field

status filters

rating filters

show results
```

The title must:

- be horizontally centered;
- have clear visual hierarchy;
- feel intentional rather than being positioned close to the status bar;
- use the existing semantic typography/design tokens.

Do not add a subtitle unless one already has a clear purpose.

Keep the header compact and clean.

---

# 5. Home Search and Filters

Search should appear immediately below the title.

Filters should appear below Search with clear spacing and grouping.

Suggested hierarchy:

```text
Show Explorer

[ Search shows... ]

Status
[ All ] [ Running ] [ Ended ] [ To Be Determined ]

Rating
[ Any ] [ 6+ ] [ 7+ ] [ 8+ ] [ 9+ ]
```

Maintain existing filtering behavior.

This task changes presentation, not filtering semantics.

---

# 6. Do Not Use "TBD" or "TDB"

Do not display:

```text
TBD
```

or:

```text
TDB
```

as the user-facing status-filter label.

Use:

```text
To Be Determined
```

in full.

The internal domain value may remain:

```ts
'to-be-determined';
```

Do not change the internal domain simply to change the UI label.

Also review `ShowStatusBadge` and other user-facing status presentation for consistency.

If this status appears elsewhere as an unclear abbreviation, use the full readable label there as well.

---

# 7. Filter Layout

Because `To Be Determined` is longer, ensure filter Chips remain usable on smaller screens.

Use an appropriate mobile layout such as:

- horizontal scrolling;
- wrapping;

depending on the existing implementation.

Avoid compressed text or clipped Chips.

Do not shrink typography excessively just to fit one line.

---

# 8. Icon System

Standardize application icons using Expo Vector Icons.

Use the icon library already available through the Expo ecosystem rather than text symbols or inconsistent icon implementations.

Inspect the currently installed packages first.

Do not install another icon library if Expo Vector Icons is already available.

---

# 9. Favorite Icon

Replace the existing heart icon with a cleaner, modern heart from Expo Vector Icons.

Use consistent states:

```text
not favorite
→ outlined heart

favorite
→ filled heart
```

Choose icons from the same icon family.

For example, an appropriate Expo Vector Icons family may expose equivalent outlined/filled heart icons.

Do not use:

- Unicode hearts;
- emoji hearts;
- different icon families for selected/unselected state.

---

# 10. Tab Icons

Review Home and Favorites tab icons as part of the same icon standardization.

Use one consistent Expo Vector Icons family where practical.

Expected semantic direction:

```text
Home
→ home outline / filled variant

Favorites
→ heart outline / filled variant
```

Selected and unselected states should feel like part of the same visual system.

Preserve existing Favorites count/badge behavior.

---

# 11. Icon Sizing

Create visual consistency between:

- tab icons;
- FavoriteButton;
- navigation actions;
- any other primary application icons.

Do not make every icon exactly the same size if context differs, but use a coherent scale.

Icons should have:

- adequate touch target;
- consistent stroke/visual weight;
- semantic accessibility labels.

The visual icon itself may be smaller than its Pressable touch area.

---

# 12. FavoriteButton Accessibility

Preserve or improve the existing accessible behavior.

The control must continue to communicate:

```text
Add {show name} to favorites
```

or:

```text
Remove {show name} from favorites
```

Do not rely only on outline/fill or color to communicate state.

