# 15. Show Detail — Reduce Vertical Footprint

The current Show Detail top area occupies too much vertical space.

Reduce the vertical footprint of the upper Show Detail section.

Focus particularly on:

- poster/image height;
- excessive vertical padding;
- gaps between title, metadata and summary;
- oversized hero/header presentation.

Do not change the physical screen height.

Instead, make the Detail content feel more compact and allow meaningful information to appear earlier.

---

# 16. Show Detail Image

Reduce the current poster/detail-image height moderately.

Do not make it tiny.

Preserve:

- aspect ratio;
- visual prominence;
- image quality;
- stable layout.

The goal is:

```text
less dominant hero
+
more content visible above the fold
```

not:

```text
thumbnail-sized poster
```

Use existing semantic spacing/tokens where possible.

---

# 17. Show Detail Spacing

Review vertical spacing around:

```text
poster
show title
status/rating
genres
favorite action
premiere
summary
episodes heading
```

Reduce unnecessary large gaps.

Maintain clear grouping and readability.

Do not flatten all spacing into one dense block.

